From 6ff957b629d08a2239b316f31ac0c9ee58fa13a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ori Pekelman <ori@pekelman.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 20:48:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: fix cpy into strided view_2d destination
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ggml_cuda_cpy enabled cpy_scalar_transpose whenever src looked like a
"compact transpose" (nb01 == elt_size, nb02 == ne00*ne01*elt_size),
without checking the destination's layout. cpy_scalar_transpose
indexes dst as `imat*n + (ty+j)*ne00 + tx` — a contiguous write,
ignoring nb1 on dst.

For the common KV-cache pattern
  V_slot = view_2d(t_V, ne0=1, ne1=d_head, nb1=max_T*4, offset=pos*4)
  cpy(t_v_new, V_slot)
the transpose kernel was triggered because src (the matmul result)
satisfied the trivial transpose conditions. The dst is a strided
view (nb1 != ne0*elt_size), so the kernel packed the source's
d_head bytes contiguously at offset pos*4 instead of distributing
them one element per max_T-spaced row.

Symptom on Qwen2.5-1.5B inference: V-cache writes silently corrupted
every decode step; logits diverged from CPU on layer 1 onward.

Fix: also require ggml_is_contiguous(src1) before enabling the
transpose path. Falls back to the general cpy_scalar kernel which
correctly uses dst strides nb10/nb11/nb12/nb13.

Repro: tinynn/ab_smoke_cpy_strided_{cpu,cuda}.rb in
oripekelman/toy_ruby_neural_network@46a61c0 — pre-patch CPU and
CUDA diverge; post-patch they agree.

Filed upstream as ggml-org/ggml#1497.
---
 src/ggml-cuda/cpy.cu | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ggml-cuda/cpy.cu b/src/ggml-cuda/cpy.cu
index d208acf..f1235f4 100644
--- a/src/ggml-cuda/cpy.cu
+++ b/src/ggml-cuda/cpy.cu
@@ -404,8 +404,13 @@ void ggml_cuda_cpy(ggml_backend_cuda_context & ctx, const ggml_tensor * src0, gg
     char * src1_ddc = (char *) src1->data;
 
     const bool contiguous_srcs = ggml_is_contiguous(src0) && ggml_is_contiguous(src1);
+    // cpy_scalar_transpose writes dst contiguously (no nb1[i] strides) — it
+    // is only correct when dst itself is contiguous. Without this guard, a
+    // strided dst (e.g. view_2d into a KV-cache slot) gets its source bytes
+    // packed at offset 0 instead of distributed across rows.
     const bool can_be_transposed = nb01 == (int64_t)ggml_element_size(src0) &&
-        src0->ne[3] == 1 && nb02 == ne00 * ne01 * (int64_t)ggml_element_size(src0);
+        src0->ne[3] == 1 && nb02 == ne00 * ne01 * (int64_t)ggml_element_size(src0) &&
+        ggml_is_contiguous(src1);
 
     if (src0->type == src1->type && contiguous_srcs) {
         GGML_ASSERT(ggml_nbytes(src0) == ggml_nbytes(src1));
-- 
